00:16:01,846 --> 00:16:07,820
after an earlier incident. The release
job runs git log --oneline --cherry-pick

211
00:16:07,860 --> 00:16:13,606
--right-only --no-merges main...release/2.3
and fails if it prints anything.

212
00:16:13,646 --> 00:16:19,315
It printed one line. The release manager
ported the commit to main with git

213
00:16:19,355 --> 00:16:24,644
cherry-pick -x, the job went green,
and 2.4.0 was tagged an hour late.

214
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:29,416
The team also knows the gate's limit: when
a port needed conflict resolution, the

215
00:16:29,456 --> 00:16:33,777
job prints the commit although it was
ported, and a person confirms from the -x

216
00:16:33,817 --> 00:16:34,053
line.

