226
00:17:26,189 --> 00:17:31,231
Answer out loud. The question has a fixed
shape: two conventions, and for each three

227
00:17:31,271 --> 00:17:36,312
things. A strong answer names each convention
with the commit it produces, one ID or

228
00:17:36,352 --> 00:17:40,910
one per line. It gives each invariant
as a command whose result a CI job can

229
00:17:40,950 --> 00:17:45,931
evaluate. And for each test it names a case
where the result is wrong in a specific

230
00:17:45,971 --> 00:17:50,891
direction: one test can say "missing" for
a fix that is present, the other can say

231
00:17:50,931 --> 00:17:53,069
